<h2>Best Roofing Materials for Central Texas Homes</h2>
<p>There isn't one right answer. The best roofing materials for Central Texas homes depend on your budget, how long you plan to stay, your home's style and how much hail protection matters to you. Here's a general comparison:</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Material</th><th>Strengths</th><th>Trade-offs</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Architectural asphalt shingles</td><td>Most common choice, wide color selection, moderate cost</td><td>Granules wear under intense sun; hail can bruise the mat</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Impact-resistant (Class 4 rated) shingles</td><td>Tested to resist hail impact better than standard shingles; some insurers offer premium discounts</td><td>Higher upfront cost; still not hail-proof</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Standing seam metal</td><td>Long service life, sheds heat and rain well, low maintenance</td><td>Higher upfront cost; large hail can dent panels cosmetically</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Stone-coated or exposed-fastener metal</td><td>Durable middle ground for some homes and outbuildings</td><td>Fasteners and seals need periodic checks</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p>For a deeper look at the two most common options, see our <a href="/services/asphalt-shingle-roofing-temple-tx/">asphalt shingle roofing</a> and <a href="/services/metal-roofing-temple-tx/">metal roofing</a> pages. Ask your insurance agent whether impact-resistant materials affect your premium before you decide.</p>

<h2>What Affects the Cost of a New Roof</h2>
<p>Cost commonly depends on roof size, pitch, the number of layers being removed, how much decking needs replacement, the complexity of valleys and penetrations, and the material selected. Steeper roofs take more time and safety equipment. Our <a href="/tools/roof-replacement-cost-calculator/">roof replacement cost calculator</a> gives a rough planning range, and the <a href="/tools/roof-pitch-calculator/">roof pitch calculator</a> helps you understand how slope factors in. For a fuller explanation, read <a href="/blog/new-roof-cost-temple-texas/">how much a new roof costs in Temple</a>. Your written estimate from the free inspection is the number that actually applies to your home.</p>

<h2>Local Weather and Timing in Bell County</h2>
<p>Central Texas puts a roof through extremes. Spring storm season, roughly March through June, brings the highest risk of hail and damaging wind, with a second round of storms often arriving in the fall. Summers routinely push into the upper 90s and above, and that heat and UV exposure age shingles faster than in milder climates. Occasional hard freezes, like the February 2021 winter storm, add another stress.</p>
<p>Those conditions shape how we install a roof: attention to attic ventilation to reduce trapped heat, proper sealing of shingle strips so they bond in warm weather, and secure edge and ridge details to resist wind. Scheduling matters too. After a large hailstorm, demand rises quickly across Temple, Belton and Harker Heights, so getting an inspection early helps you plan rather than wait.</p>

<h2>When to Have Your Roof Evaluated for Replacement</h2>
<p>Schedule an inspection if your roof is approaching the later part of its expected life, if you're buying or selling a home, after any storm that left damage in your neighborhood, or if you've needed more than one repair in a short span. An honest evaluation sometimes shows you have years left; other times it confirms that replacement now will prevent costlier interior damage later. Either way, you'll know where you stand.</p>
